{
 "about": "Hand marks on printed parts' edges, in pixels of 1920x1080 frames of the Prusa CORE One's camera, from the frame-panels spike. Each curve's points lie on the planned outline `what` names at height `z` (`top`: that layer's outer walls; `first`: every first-layer extrusion, the brim included), and `zc_mm` is the height the print had reached when the frame was taken, which the bed had dropped by. The spike's sheet-corner, hole and printed-mark points are left out: a sheet sits up to 4.7 mm apart between prints, so they anchor nothing. Its one 1280x720 frame (fan-cut-bridge) is left out too: a calibration is for one resolution.",
